<details><summary>Why expected log size, rather than log average size?</summary>
After observing $b$, the conditional source is uniform on the actual fiber $f^{-1}(b)$, whose entropy is $\log|f^{-1}(b)|$. Conditional entropy averages these logarithms using the output probabilities. Moving the logarithm outside the expectation would describe a different statistic and would break the exact chain rule for unequal fibers.
